en:
It was wrapped in darkness and he couldn't make it out clearly, but he could see someone's figure.
Dimly, a black shadow was crouched by the wall, squirming and wriggling.
It looked like a person, and it also looked like a lump of flesh.{p}

Don't turn around.
That's what he told himself.
Then, somehow steadying his breathing, he stood up again and slowly started walking.{p}

Even so, you didn't look back.
Because you listened to her advice.
Because you kept your promise to her.{p}

Thank you.
Actually, there's something else I want to ask you.
Something very important.{p}

Thank you.
Actually, there's something else I want to ask you.
Something very important.{p}

Thank you.
You're a good person, aren't you?
Then I'll ask you my last question.{p}

That won't do.
You see, I want you to be someone who can listen to other people's advice.
Why would I say that to you, when we've only just met?{p}

I thought you'd answer that way.
Heh heh...
Then I'll begin my story.{p}

I thought you'd answer that way.
Heh heh...
Then I'll begin my story.{p}

You decided to go out with her.
After all, as you'd expect of a girl who had watched you from afar all that time, she was very modest and sweet.
You knew nothing of the terrible feelings that had taken root in her heart.{p}

Even so, you kept going out with her.
Because she was a really good girl.
...Except that she killed every mosquito that sucked your blood, one by one.{p}

She thought:
Rather than let the mosquitoes keep sucking my {a}'s blood like this...
I might as well, I might as well just...{p}

It was dark underfoot on the stairs, and it felt somehow as if he were descending into darkness itself.
When he reached the floor below, the first thing he looked at was the classroom at the end of the hallway.
And then...{p}

He had a bad feeling, somehow.
He sensed an unusual aura about these stairs.
So he decided to go through the hallway in front of him and take the stairs at the far end.{p}

He listened hard.........
He heard nothing.
He must have been hearing things because he was so scared.{p}

Terrified, he broke into a run.
Who could blame him?
He tore down the hallway at full speed, so fast he could barely breathe.{p}

Her withered hand reached out to grab him.
It's all over!
He braced himself for the end.{p}

But just then......
The hand she had stretched out crumbled away.
From the fingertips, as if it were turning to sand.{p}

And he saw them.
The creatures chasing him, crumbling to pieces as they ran.
Their faces as they turned into piles of sand, staring at him with longing and resentment.{p}

What do you think you're doing?
Turn around?
You said you'd turn around?{p}

You turned around.
Of course, she was furious.
Letting out a howl of wordless rage, she strangled you.{p}
